00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.400
Be careful with what I ask for, we will apply midocaine to him.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.600
You forgot to put on the jacket.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.600
I'll tell you later.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.600
Oxygenation, 92 in 4 liters.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.400
Does he take any medication? Does he suffer from any allergy?

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.600
No, miserable pigs, only, only give me a calmant.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.100
4 milligrams of morphine.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.700
You win, friend, morphine.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.730
I've seen her before, in the cafeteria.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.430
Exactly, and before that, on the train, do you remember?

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.640
- She works here. - Is she the administrator?

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.640
Damn it!

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.000
- Mr. Thoracic ready. - Well, we proceed.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.850
Her blood pressure dropped to 70, tachycardia 130, hemorrhage, there are 1,000 cubic centimeters.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:08.730
Transfusion through the fast medium, apply what you lost and other four units.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:12.750
Dr. Cordelia will take care of another patient and I have hundreds of lacerations.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.750
We will receive more and tell the patients that we will take care of them as soon as we can.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.750
When will that patient arrive?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.760
I need help with the skater, the pain is very intense.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.760
Four of morphine, one of Bercet, I'll be right back.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.760
That patient, the doctor who has another employee.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.760
Dr. Cobart?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.760
Yes, I don't know, investigate when he should arrive.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.760
What is this?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.000
The driver of the truck.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.120
Call for transport, take him to the morgue.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.300
Hey, is that you, Doctor?

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.900
I have a damn migraine, I'm going crazy.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.640
We'll take care of it as soon as we can.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:42.300
I applied for a compassine, it's a suppository, but it didn't help at all, nothing. What can you give me?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.600
Take a seat, we'll take care of it in a minute.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.500
That's what they said 20 minutes ago.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.900
I assure you they will.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:52.670
Doctor Weaver, phone.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:54.870
Peter, can you continue here? I'm going to see Elizabeth.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.470
Yes, we're waiting for a operating room.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.180
Carol?

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.000
Please!

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:04.150
I don't know what happened to her. I don't know where she is.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.630
What's her name? I'll look for her.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.370
Michelle. Michelle Keeney.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.380
You'd better take care of that first.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.300
