00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.020
- I don't inform the residents. - And I hope to have it on my desk.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.000
- Why would he do that? - I don't know.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.120
Something about the annoying daily routine of his position.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.930
How are you doing, Cartel?

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.330
Prepare him for the operating room.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.610
I do not understand, is it so difficult to give me something for the pain?

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.170
I'm sorry, ma'am, we are attending to delicate patients.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.200
And this damn jaqueca is not serious?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.600
What kind of damn tufurio is this?

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.720
Randy, do you want to kill the one with the migraine?

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:18.680
Will it be a pleasure?

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:22.090
A little girl arrived with this accident, five years old, Michelle Keeney.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:22.890
I did not see her.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.770
I could be on my way, I just hung up with the network.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.810
They will send me two critical patients in ten minutes.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.000
What do you mean? I told you that we would not receive more.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.340
I don't know, but Dr. Romano approved it.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.340
Who asked you?

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.000
I did. I followed the protocol. He's the head of the department.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.260
Call the radio and tell them to go to Mercy and locate Romano on the phone.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:42.480
What the hell is going on? We can barely get ahead with this.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.370
The pressure is 375.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.830
Other two units of O negative. There is no hemorrhage in the vein.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.750
The x-ray shows concussions on both sides of the heart.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.250
There are no traces of hemorrhage.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.430
Oxygenation 80% to 100% oxygen.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.350
I will check the heart.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:57.230
It could be a collapsed lung.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.540
Throat of 14 in open syringe.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:00.890
It's written 42.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.850
There's no fusion in the pericardium.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.860
Nor pulmonary tension.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.800
But there's a severe failure of injection.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.860
Due to cardiac contusion.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.860
There's a strong trauma in heart and lungs.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:14.860
Another 5 of pressure.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.970
Arterial pressure in 60.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:17.970
Prepare a dose of dopamine.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:18.970
I go to the operating room.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.970
There's no surgical preparation.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.690
You're right, unfortunately.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.680
What do we do?

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.690
Pressure and support with fan and that's all.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:28.690
No, wait a minute, run to the operating room.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.000
I want to try something, quickly.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:34.430
Bring the bypass machine. Surgery tray. We'll prepare it for a bypass catheter.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.430
I'll practice a bypass. It's very risky.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.310
It's worth trying.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.290
Betadine and sterile gases.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.290
Wow, wow, wow. This is a convention.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.290
Charlie Cameron! Are you still in Rush?

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.140
-Cohete? -I hadn't seen you in...

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.140
Oh, heavens, who cares?

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.100
What brings you to these places?

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.810
Your coffee, of course.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:56.210
They say it's the best in town.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.210
Well, there are too many cooks for this dinner.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.000
I'll go inspire the rest...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.950
I'm going to take care of the troop.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.190
Typhoon ready.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.830
Oxygenation 99%.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:05.670
Peter, what's going on here?

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:09.470
Penetrating trauma in the thorax, 1000 cc of bleeding, we'll take him to the typhoon.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.590
Uh-huh, what's the pressure?

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.230
95, assist him, starting from 70.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.590
Stop, stop, he'll stay here.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.200
What?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:14.880
Watch the pressure.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.630
Requires thoracotomy.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.670
A liter of blood when intubated indicates that it must be intervened.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.150
No, it's on the limit, how much blood has been applied?

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.770
Two units of O negative, auto-transfusion.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.440
What's in the thoracic seal?

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.000
100 cubic centimeters.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.250
Uh-huh, and the pressure?

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:29.370
105 over 74.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.000
Good.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.400
Peter, let's analyze, his blood pressure is in the normal range and the bleeding has decreased to a minimum.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.700
As a surgeon, I would say that he is forming a clot.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.820
As a trauma specialist, would you disagree?

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:40.420
Maybe.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:46.120
Maybe. Well, if we are going to open his chest, exposing him to the risks of anesthesia and subject him to a painful six-month recovery,

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.420
let's make sure that a "maybe" is not part of the equation.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:49.120
Thank you.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.050
Hi, what's your name?

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:06.910
My name is Luca.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:09.310
It's very curious, isn't it?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.780
Can you say it, Luca?

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:16.000
Does your arm hurt?

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:21.040
I'm the doctor.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.990
I want my mom.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:29.060
Can I help you?

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.000
Don't you want to get off the elevator?

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:35.900
In that case, would you mind if I go up?

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:42.510
Yes, of course, Lucy. It will be a pleasure to support you.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.850
- Hello! - I'm pleasing your interest.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.890
- I'm agonizing, some imbecile is interested! - Thank you, Mr. Rubius.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:51.220
I wanted to focus on traumatology in my last year and I think it would be great to have a good idea.

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.600
I know that will be so. I had a great teacher when I was studying.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.460
What do you want, huh? Do I need to be shot?

00:11:56.460 --> 00:12:00.000
- Finish with the patient and send the other for a tomography. - Thank you, Carter.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.720
Do you know the rumor that Dr. Anspog will resign as head of staff?

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.240
No, where did you hear that?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:10.540
I heard something terrifying, not only will Dr. Anspog resign, but Dr. Romano will be the candidate to replace him.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.540
Romano as head of staff?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.730
Katia, I'll see you on Saturday.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.550
Are you okay?

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.570
Prepare the palettes. Malik, get the compresses ready.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:20.910
I'm coming, connect this.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:24.230
Marc, you have a minute, I need to talk to you, it's important.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:24.730
Sure.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:25.230
I have nine.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:28.670
Charge 200.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:29.600
Start bypass.

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:53.180
Very well. Do you want to talk here?

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:54.560
Reduce dopamine.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.390
Pressure 120/80.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:13:00.000
They say Anspor will give up and that Romano could take his place.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:03.260
No, it's not possible, ANSPOC would have told us something.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.160
You're right, maybe it's just a rumor without a foundation.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.260
I'll go see him in a moment to talk to him.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.360
Great idea.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:09.920
What the hell?

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:11.420
It's the alarm against fire!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:13.020
