00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:04.150
that tutor? I will have it. And if you don't get it, what are you going to learn? Signs in

00:29:04.150 --> 00:29:07.290
language? Please, the objective of this session, and remember, are the

00:29:07.290 --> 00:29:12.010
needs. You need to be with your mother. You need to be with your father. Yes, what

00:29:12.010 --> 00:29:15.850
will you do? Will you take him home when you leave the hospital to lay him on the sofa

00:29:15.850 --> 00:29:23.460
of your room? He has no room? Of course yes. Since when? We moved with my

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:30.000
sister Jackie and her family so that Ruiz can have a unit

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:32.060
A more complete family.

00:29:32.060 --> 00:29:34.230
She would have her with us.

00:29:34.230 --> 00:29:37.840
Her black mother and her black stepfather.

00:29:37.840 --> 00:29:39.840
What the hell are you talking about?

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:41.840
What happens if I go out with a white woman?

00:29:41.840 --> 00:29:47.400
I was just saying...

00:29:47.400 --> 00:29:49.400
Listen, I can't do this.

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:51.320
Yes, you can. The court ordered it.

00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:52.320
Don't forget it.

00:29:52.320 --> 00:30:00.000
What is the diagnosis?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.820
Fantastic.

00:30:01.820 --> 00:30:02.820
What are you doing here?

00:30:02.820 --> 00:30:06.800
You said you'd wait in reception and I found this chair.

00:30:06.800 --> 00:30:09.100
I didn't know we had it.

00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:09.920
That's mine.

00:30:09.920 --> 00:30:22.330
Yes?

00:30:22.330 --> 00:30:23.330
It doesn't seem to be a hand.

00:30:23.330 --> 00:30:24.510
Or yes?

00:30:24.510 --> 00:30:25.850
No.

00:30:25.850 --> 00:30:27.920
At least what a hand can do.

00:30:31.690 --> 00:30:33.410
It's in Larguirucha.

00:30:33.410 --> 00:30:35.450
At least there's no fracture.

00:30:35.450 --> 00:30:38.010
That's good.

00:30:38.010 --> 00:30:39.130
Can I go now?

00:30:39.130 --> 00:30:41.340
I'll come with you.

00:30:41.340 --> 00:30:43.170
Do you need help?

00:30:43.170 --> 00:30:45.670
I'll be traveling in a taxi until I fix my car.

00:30:45.670 --> 00:30:47.550
Ah.

00:30:47.550 --> 00:30:50.300
I trusted something a little more dramatic.

00:30:50.300 --> 00:30:52.500
A chiseled arm, a headscarf maybe.

00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:55.510
Something to not go to the charity function that I promised tonight.

00:30:55.510 --> 00:30:56.510
Ah, don't tell me.

00:30:56.510 --> 00:30:57.510
Exactly.

00:30:57.510 --> 00:30:59.110
The Carter family foundation.

00:30:59.110 --> 00:31:00.000
Despite the divorce,

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:07.590
- Why do you never attend these functions? - Oh, I managed to get rid of his claws.

00:31:07.590 --> 00:31:13.640
- What are they doing tonight? Will they save a lake? No, no, the children's library? - Almost, a children's garden.

00:31:13.640 --> 00:31:17.450
- Randy, do you want to get a taxi for Miss Nichols? - Sure.

00:31:17.450 --> 00:31:23.160
- Thank you, Dr. Carter. - It's a pleasure, a pleasure, and I'll be thinking about you.

00:31:23.160 --> 00:31:27.940
- Will you do it? - I mean tonight, while you greet the rest of the Carters.

00:31:27.940 --> 00:31:30.000
- So...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.140
Then I'll think of you too.

00:31:34.150 --> 00:31:35.060
Nice to meet you.

00:31:39.300 --> 00:31:42.060
I hope Anspo hasn't made a decision.

00:31:42.060 --> 00:31:46.060
If there are enough votes against Romano, how could you name him Anspo?

00:31:46.060 --> 00:31:48.060
Will we be enough? That's the question.

00:31:48.060 --> 00:31:49.060
Do you think we could be just you and me?

00:31:49.060 --> 00:31:51.170
You don't even think about that.

00:31:51.170 --> 00:31:54.100
We know he's anxious, even desperate.

00:31:54.100 --> 00:31:56.920
So there's no reason not to support him.

00:31:56.920 --> 00:32:00.000
Although, as head of radiology,

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:07.190
I would like to comment that no boss in this area has been considered for the head of staff, maybe it's a topic for another occasion.

00:32:07.190 --> 00:32:09.190
I understand why they take so long to interpret the plates.

00:32:09.190 --> 00:32:11.310
Thank you Steve, Carl?

00:32:11.310 --> 00:32:20.540
I am the head of psychiatry and it took six months for me to know that Donald was at the front, if it does not affect my world, Dr. Romano is a good choice.

00:32:20.540 --> 00:32:24.090
What do you say Jack?

00:32:24.090 --> 00:32:30.000
You know I like you Donald, I'm fed up with so much bureaucratic garbage, I already suffered a cardiac attack.

00:32:30.860 --> 00:32:34.560
If there is anyone willing to accept the position, welcome.

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:40.730
Mark?

00:32:40.730 --> 00:32:49.010
Well, I hate to be the discerning voice, and it is not something personal, Robert, but I want to be honest...

00:32:49.010 --> 00:32:51.650
Absolutely.

00:32:51.650 --> 00:32:58.450
As head of the emergency area during the last few months, Dr. Romano has...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:19.330
He has not provided us with a great support, his administrative style is, I would say, abrupt and several members of our staff have, well, they have considered him offensive.

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:24.310
Continue.

00:33:24.310 --> 00:33:29.860
I feel that I would worry that Doctor Romano

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:32.880
I had the control of all the staff and teachers.

00:33:38.230 --> 00:33:42.640
Well, I appreciate your sincerity, Kerry.

00:33:45.550 --> 00:33:48.350
Any of us who have been administrators know that

00:33:48.870 --> 00:33:51.370
it is not easy to get to a new department.

00:33:51.370 --> 00:33:55.080
I agree with Mark, there have been some stumbles along the way,

00:33:55.380 --> 00:34:00.000
but I think that Dr. Romano has managed to stabilize the situation.

00:34:01.310 --> 00:34:04.910
And now he brings a genuine leadership to the emergency department.

00:34:04.910 --> 00:34:09.410
Would you give him your support as head of staff?

00:34:09.410 --> 00:34:12.410
It would be fair to give him all of our support.

00:34:12.410 --> 00:34:21.110
You left me alone, Kerry.

00:34:21.110 --> 00:34:25.120
Mark, I'm sorry, but it was obvious that Roman would stay in the position.

00:34:25.120 --> 00:34:28.620
Imagine what it could be against Urgencia if we both were against each other.

00:34:28.620 --> 00:34:30.000
It didn't seem opportune to me.

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:34.230
Oh, I see. You were smart while I risked my life being stupid and honest.

00:34:34.230 --> 00:34:37.630
Oh, enough. I was just trying to protect the apartment.

00:34:37.630 --> 00:34:39.930
Maybe you believe it, Kerry, but don't ask me the same thing.

00:34:39.930 --> 00:34:43.570
Donald's meetings are so boring that we all need coffee, right?

00:34:43.570 --> 00:34:52.790
Well, how about it? I decided to get my old scraper. New image for a new job.

00:34:52.790 --> 00:34:57.840
Oh, I'm going to work. Kerry, if you have a minute, I'd like to tell you something.

00:35:08.830 --> 00:35:10.830
Hey, didn't I leave my glasses at your house?

00:35:10.830 --> 00:35:12.230
I don't know, we can look for them.

00:35:12.230 --> 00:35:14.150
Sure, go on. And what did he say?

00:35:14.150 --> 00:35:16.150
He said it would be difficult to locate Carlos.

00:35:16.150 --> 00:35:17.450
For being a positive zero?

00:35:17.450 --> 00:35:20.650
Exactly, and I couldn't tell them that, I ordered the analysis illegally.

00:35:20.650 --> 00:35:22.650
They don't care, they administer the cocktail.

00:35:22.650 --> 00:35:23.620
I know.

00:35:23.620 --> 00:35:28.230
Although I think I would be the perfect adoptive mother for that baby,

00:35:28.230 --> 00:35:30.000
I can face the HIV.

00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:32.150
You're right, you'd be perfect.

00:35:32.150 --> 00:35:34.950
That's not what the agency thinks, considering that I'm a positive being.

00:35:34.950 --> 00:35:36.590
You're healthier than many others.

00:35:36.590 --> 00:35:37.950
Yes, but I'm not married.

00:35:37.950 --> 00:35:40.390
Not yet.

00:35:40.390 --> 00:35:44.690
So there's no support system for the baby if something happens to me.

00:35:44.690 --> 00:35:45.610
Not yet.

00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:46.550
Reggie...

00:35:46.550 --> 00:35:48.940
We can solve that part right now.

00:35:48.940 --> 00:35:50.840
I have to go back, let's drink our coffee.

00:35:50.840 --> 00:35:52.790
No, tell her you'll marry me.

00:35:52.790 --> 00:35:53.670
Reggie...

00:35:53.670 --> 00:35:54.730
Don't you think I'm serious?

00:35:54.730 --> 00:35:57.780
I think you're crazy.

00:36:00.800 --> 00:36:04.610
Ginny Boulay, do you want to be my wife?

00:36:04.610 --> 00:36:11.230
Congratulations, Dr. Green.

00:36:11.230 --> 00:36:12.130
What's all this about?

00:36:12.130 --> 00:36:13.440
Your meeting with Anspach.

00:36:13.440 --> 00:36:14.610
How did you find out?

00:36:14.610 --> 00:36:15.810
The nurses know everything.

00:36:15.810 --> 00:36:17.510
I see you for a good cause. Thank you, Mark.

00:36:17.510 --> 00:36:19.120
I doubt it will help us.

00:36:19.120 --> 00:36:20.580
Mark, do you have a minute?

00:36:20.580 --> 00:36:22.380
I was about to leave.

00:36:22.380 --> 00:36:25.240
Listen, I think we should talk.

00:36:25.240 --> 00:36:26.640
I think we already did, Carrie.

00:36:26.640 --> 00:36:28.160
It's about something different.

00:36:31.180 --> 00:36:38.180
A woman of 30 years, pregnant, ADA, occupied the passenger seat, without pulse in the ambulance, cardiac arrest 10 minutes ago, we could not intubate.

00:36:38.180 --> 00:36:39.560
One, two, three.

00:36:39.560 --> 00:36:41.150
Heavens, she's about to give birth.

00:36:41.150 --> 00:36:42.630
Chuni, continue the animation.

00:36:42.630 --> 00:36:46.150
I need a tube of 8 and a little suction.

00:36:46.150 --> 00:36:49.570
Prepare a central catheter, four units of O negative and look for another doctor.

00:36:49.570 --> 00:36:51.540
Jale, check the fetal heartbeat.

00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:52.810
Assist the monitor.

00:36:52.810 --> 00:36:54.210
Start cricoid pressure.

00:36:54.210 --> 00:36:55.610
The venoclisis came out.

00:36:55.610 --> 00:36:57.530
Very well, I'm in.

00:36:57.530 --> 00:36:59.280
A pineprine ampoule in the tube.

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:01.120
The blood has arrived!

00:37:01.120 --> 00:37:03.120
Use the fast method, I'll get a subclavia.

00:37:03.120 --> 00:37:05.320
It's a terminal pregnancy, fetal heartbeat?

00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:06.320
I can't find it.

00:37:06.320 --> 00:37:07.320
What is the mother's rhythm?

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:08.820
I'm assisting her, she's intubated.

00:37:08.820 --> 00:37:10.120
Was there a pulse in transit?

00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:11.120
The paramedic said no.

00:37:11.120 --> 00:37:12.030
How long?

00:37:12.030 --> 00:37:13.560
12 minutes already.

00:37:13.560 --> 00:37:14.600
The mother died.

00:37:14.600 --> 00:37:15.600
Wait, we couldn't try...

00:37:15.600 --> 00:37:17.600
You know she's dead, we have to get the baby out.

00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:19.600
Subclavia ready, apply the units.

00:37:20.160 --> 00:37:21.680
Chuny, keep the compresses.

00:37:21.680 --> 00:37:23.180
I need retractors.

00:37:23.180 --> 00:37:24.680
Bring an incubator!

00:37:24.680 --> 00:37:25.530
Incision drawer!

00:37:25.530 --> 00:37:27.240
There's no time, give me your hands.

00:37:30.830 --> 00:37:32.070
-You have to open it. -Yes.

00:37:32.130 --> 00:37:34.420
He had a heart attack. He's a 32-year-old Frenchman.

00:37:34.420 --> 00:37:35.830
I'm opening his uterus.

00:37:35.830 --> 00:37:38.270
Bandages.

00:37:38.290 --> 00:37:41.030
We're going to suction him.

00:37:41.040 --> 00:37:52.980
He's a kid.

00:38:26.040 --> 00:38:27.240
I'm going to go with the compresses.

00:38:27.560 --> 00:38:28.960
Follow the system.

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:30.000
Once again.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.000
A drop of atropine, repeat the epinephrine, and Chuni continues with the reanimation.

00:38:34.610 --> 00:38:36.530
The heartbeat in 140.

00:38:36.530 --> 00:38:38.060
What color do you have?

00:38:38.060 --> 00:38:40.060
Calification of Asgard, 8 out of 10.

00:38:40.060 --> 00:38:41.560
Enough.

00:38:41.560 --> 00:38:45.340
Yes.

00:38:45.340 --> 00:38:47.520
Time of death, 18:48.

00:39:07.550 --> 00:39:10.440
-How is he? -Better.

00:39:10.440 --> 00:39:12.650
-He had a fever. Now he's resting well.

00:39:12.650 --> 00:39:15.340
-Good. Is there anything about his mother?

00:39:15.340 --> 00:39:19.860
-No. I didn't know they were in the final stage.

00:39:19.860 --> 00:39:25.710
-Yes. We're going to give him the triple cocktail.

00:39:25.710 --> 00:39:29.120
-They haven't done any analysis.

00:39:29.120 --> 00:39:30.000
-Give it to him, Kit.

00:39:31.400 --> 00:39:39.230
- Okay. - Randy, did you see Dr. Green?

00:39:39.230 --> 00:39:41.900
- He left. - Hey Carter, do you have a minute?

00:39:41.900 --> 00:39:45.960
- Yes, sure. I heard it was true, the rumor that Romano will be the boss.

00:39:45.960 --> 00:39:51.460
- Yes, although he has not made the official announcement, he named me head of emergencies.

00:39:51.460 --> 00:39:54.260
- While he continues his eternal search for someone permanent.

00:39:54.260 --> 00:39:56.540
- No, in fact, I plan to stay.

00:39:56.540 --> 00:40:00.000
- Hey, bravo! Congratulations! - Thank you.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:05.140
thank you for telling me but what I wanted to tell you is that I do not think it is

00:40:05.140 --> 00:40:11.180
prudent that you continue to rent my apartment I feel that whoever occupies it

00:40:11.180 --> 00:40:16.690
should not belong to the hospital is asking me to move yes of course take

00:40:16.690 --> 00:40:25.070
your time a week or two look for something not only accommodated this game of

00:40:25.070 --> 00:40:30.000
sutura I know that those that are open are not preserved but the scissors are not used

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:34.000
the forceps, it seems to me a great waste to throw them away.

00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:37.320
Do you feel good?

00:40:37.320 --> 00:40:40.600
You mean childbirth? Yes, I'm lucky.

00:40:40.600 --> 00:40:41.810
Really?

00:40:41.810 --> 00:40:47.720
You know, Luca, despite what they think, he's a good doctor.

00:40:47.720 --> 00:40:51.450
Thank you.

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:08.640
What did you tell me? I'll think about you tonight?

00:41:08.640 --> 00:41:11.600
It was the truth.

00:41:11.600 --> 00:41:14.190
Do you like jeeps?

00:41:14.190 --> 00:41:16.360
It's not a BMW.

00:41:16.360 --> 00:41:18.980
Well, it's not a taxi, right?

00:41:18.980 --> 00:41:20.920
I like jeeps.

00:41:20.920 --> 00:41:22.880
I thought we could go for a drink.

00:41:22.880 --> 00:41:25.960
That's not what I want.

00:41:30.860 --> 00:41:32.700
Dr. Weaver, can I talk to you for a second?

00:41:32.700 --> 00:41:35.100
I examined patient 4's anaphylactic.

00:41:35.100 --> 00:41:38.280
Her breathing and pulse were stabilized, so she will recover.

00:41:38.280 --> 00:41:42.660
The patient with hematuria will be hospitalized and we will raise the case of dermatitis.

00:41:42.660 --> 00:41:43.420
Excellent.

00:41:43.420 --> 00:41:46.300
I wanted to know if I should read something in particular tonight.

00:41:46.300 --> 00:41:51.590
Um, Lucy, I'm sorry, I'm afraid I won't be able to continue helping you.

00:41:51.590 --> 00:41:55.380
I've just been appointed as head of the emergency department.

00:41:55.380 --> 00:41:57.470
But that's good, isn't it?

00:41:57.470 --> 00:42:00.000
Yes, but it would be considered

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:03.040
As a favoritism, you have to advise only one student.

00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:05.620
Talk to Dr. Green. Maybe he has time.

00:42:05.620 --> 00:42:08.100
Dr. Weaver, Randy has a call for Dr. Green.

00:42:08.100 --> 00:42:09.700
Give me the message. Has he left?

00:42:09.700 --> 00:42:11.640
I think he needs to be treated. It's his father.

00:42:11.640 --> 00:42:18.760
He said Dr. Green's mother just passed away.

00:42:18.760 --> 00:42:21.830
Hello, this is Kerry Weaver. Can I help you?

00:42:32.840 --> 00:42:36.760
So this is what men do to get rid of their anger and frustration.

00:42:36.760 --> 00:42:42.670
I thought that killing Romano and Weaver would be very scandalous.

00:42:42.670 --> 00:42:46.780
How did you do with me?

00:42:46.780 --> 00:42:52.430
I have my sources. I know what you did in the meeting with Aspen.

00:42:52.430 --> 00:42:55.900
What I did was to end my career.

00:42:55.900 --> 00:42:59.620
I opened the door for Carrie to become a boss.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:02.860
Your opinion in front of Romano required a lot of courage.

00:43:02.860 --> 00:43:06.840
If it helps you, I'm proud of what you did.

00:43:06.840 --> 00:43:11.400
Thank you.

00:43:11.400 --> 00:43:14.080
And how is this about hitting the ball like that?

00:43:14.080 --> 00:43:15.620
It doesn't seem that difficult.

00:43:15.620 --> 00:43:18.930
Ah, that's what you think, huh?

00:43:18.930 --> 00:43:20.490
You seem to be doing it.

00:43:20.490 --> 00:43:23.880
Would you like to try it?

00:43:23.880 --> 00:43:25.010
Let's go.

00:43:25.010 --> 00:43:27.560
Okay.

00:43:27.560 --> 00:43:28.560
Go ahead.

00:43:28.560 --> 00:43:30.000
Do I do it like this?

00:43:31.020 --> 00:43:32.880
-Good! -Oh!

00:43:32.880 --> 00:43:34.900
-My God! -Come on, hit it!

00:43:39.410 --> 00:43:45.070
-I'm learning! -You have good eyesight.

00:43:45.070 --> 00:43:48.400
Focus on the ball.

00:43:48.400 --> 00:43:50.280
-Here it comes. -Very good!

00:43:50.280 --> 00:43:51.060
Very good!
